     1	# Proposal: Auto-detect and heal timespec/data mismatches at FolderDB open
     2	
     3	Before assignment 00004, the old global-timespec contamination bug could produce databases
     4	whose `config.meta` says `seconds` while the files actually contain microsecond-precision
     5	datetime keys (or vice versa). Such a database still loads — nothing is lost — but its
     6	datetime keys deserialize as plain strings because `_is_datetime_string` matches on exact
     7	length per configured precision.
     8	
     9	This assignment adds a guard at `FolderDB.__init__`: infer the data's actual precision from
    10	the `min_index`/`max_index` keys already recorded in `db.meta`, and when it consistently
    11	disagrees with the configured timespec, adopt the detected value, rewrite `config.meta`, and
    12	print a warning. Mixed precisions across tables keep the configured value and warn (no safe
    13	automatic choice exists). The guard is read-cheap (one `db.meta` read, no file scans) and
    14	keeps reads and writes symmetric — unlike a read-side-only fallback, which would re-serialize
    15	recovered datetime keys at the wrong precision and write them back under different keys.

